# VLB evaluation lane — running journal

2026-10-03. Worker lane task: evaluate arXiv:2602.17201 (Diaz-Dominguez &
Makinen, "Adaptive encodings for small and fast compressed suffix arrays",
VLB-tree + state-valid sampling) for the sxgc container line.

## Phase 1 — paper (DONE, see paper-notes.md)

- Fetched https://arxiv.org/pdf/2602.17201 (11-page PDF, 28pp ACM format)
  -> paper-fulltext.txt. Extracted (a)-(f) into paper-notes.md.
- Key finds: public code at github.com/ddiazdom/VLBT (live, public);
  no asymptotic space bound (open problem, their Sec 9); their "state-valid
  sampling" (Sec 5) subsamples the VLB-tree's root ROUTING arrays (Z) using
  suffix-tree overlap structure (lmo/rmo) — it does NOT subsample SA samples
  (Sec 7 reuses sr-index subsampling for those). Self-index: yes.
- Honest framing correction journaled in paper-notes.md: the set of
  backward-search interval states over ALL occurring patterns is ALL rows
  (each row is the singleton interval of its own context). The non-trivial
  restriction is the workload one (MEM minimal length L), which we
  implement exactly as V_L = rows whose L-mer occurs >= 2 times.

## Phase 2 — prototype (IN PROGRESS)

Tool: vlb_stateval.cpp (C++17, no deps) in this directory. Decoder copied
from the proven skiplist-lane tool (bit6/sxi_logs/skiplist-locate/
skiplist_locate.cpp): SXI2 codec-101 runs, member-11 anchor semantics
(one raw u64 tail-SA per 1024th run; locate walk terminates on the
anchored TAIL row; SA[origin] = (anchor + steps) mod n).

Corpora (retained artifacts, READ-ONLY):
- yeast235 v5: /mnt/nvme3n1/erikg/sxi2-v5/yeast235.sxi2
  n=3,336,986,759 R=100,905,045 member11=98,541 anchors
- pile-frag v5: /mnt/nvme3n1/erikg/sxi2-v5/pile-frag.sxi2
  n=1,082,130,213 R=397,723,010 member11=388,402 anchors

Method (all offline measurement passes, NOT proposed build steps; the
skiplist lane's sweep precedent walks the full LF cycle at this scale):
1. text = inverse BWT via anchor-segment walks (parallel), byte-compare
   vs source in ONE forward pass (THE-LAW style).
2. SA[row] via the same segment walks, seeded by member-11 anchor values.
   Gates: all 98,541 anchor values == SA[tailrow] (tautological per
   segment but catches segment-boundary/walk bugs), sum(SA)==n(n-1)/2,
   and selftest mode: exact rank vs brute, LF bijection, and
   L[i]==T[(SA[i]-1) mod n] for ALL rows (smoke corpus: all exact).
3. V_L bitmaps for L in {20,39,100}: row r in V_L iff
   LCP(SA[r-1],SA[r])>=L or LCP(SA[r],SA[r+1])>=L (cyclic).
4. ONE parallel orbit walk (orbit index of row = (A0 - SA) mod n, A0 =
   anchor_val[0]; LF decrements SA by 1): gaps between consecutive
   run-tails in orbit order + per-L valid aggregates + member-11
   uniform walk stats (must reproduce the banked lane numbers:
   yeast mean 221,573 / max 6,516,845; pile 3,050.6 / 134,859).
5. Greedy state-valid placement per L, per D (min anchor count s.t.
   every V_L point has an anchor within D ahead on the orbit), plus the
   all-rows variant (pure orbit-aware placement) and D* bisection at the
   member-11 anchor count.
6. Benchmark: 1000 patterns of length L from the text, backward search
   (exact rank, selftested), locate every sampled interval row both
   ways; gates: recovered position == SA[startrow] (exact answer parity
   vs the reconstructed SA) AND pattern-context byte match. Latency
   measured in the same run for both.

Smoke test (random-4-2k, n=2001): all gates 0 mismatches (ASAN clean).
Bug found+fixed during smoke: the interval-interior row sampler could
overshoot ep (j beyond rowCap-1) — produced false context mismatches;
rank/LF/BWT-property selftests were exact throughout.

Resource use: <= 31 threads, ~27 GB RSS peak expected for yeast.

