## Phase 2 — pile-frag results (COMPLETE, pile-frag.run.log / run2.log)

All gates green (member-11 crosscheck 388,402/388,402; sum(SA) OK;
benchmark 0 SA-parity / 0 context mismatches; orbit stats reproduce the
banked lane exactly: 3,050.6 / 134,858).

- |V_20|=28.31%, |V_31|=11.64%, |V_100|=4.03% of n — the restriction is
  real on text, unlike yeast.
- BUT anchor-count savings from state-validity are ~nil at L=20 (0.7%
  fewer than all-rows at D=4,096), 9.7% at L=31, 73% at L=100 — and the
  L=100 placement strands the singleton starts (88% of real benchmark
  starts; measured 10x WORSE locate from them: mean 33,893 steps).
- Orbit-aware all-rows placement: same count -> mean 1,415 (2.16x),
  max 97,037 (1.4x); D=1,024 -> 1.06M anchors (2.8% of the 2.05 GB lite)
  -> mean 537 (5.7x); D=256 -> 4.25M anchors (~4.1% of lite incl. bitmap)
  -> mean 158 (19.3x). Dominates the skiplist lane's jump pointers
  (47% of lite for 5.8x) on the space-time plane; composable with them.

## Phase 3 — verdict row (full arithmetic in REPORT.md)

1. Warm-form samples 1.4-2.4 TB -> 0.35-1.6 TB STANDS (sr-index
   subsampling); VLB state-valid sampling does not touch SA samples
   (it subsamples the VLB-tree Z routing arrays). VLB's warm-form value
   is layout (T_phi interleave) - a future member-8 re-encoding lane.
2. Lite locate 3.1k mean -> 1.4k at identical anchor count (2.2x); ~160
   steps at ~4% of the lite artifact (~19x) - via ORBIT-AWARE anchors,
   NOT state-validity.
3. Member 1 -> VLB tree: NO (>=13-16 bits/run vs 7.2; satellite overhead
   maximal at n/r=2.85; their own HUM already loses to fbb by 13-18%;
   expected pile VLB BWT ~1-1.6 TB vs 414 GB).

Lane complete. No process left running at close; nothing staged.
